            "Jasur always wondered where his money went. He had a good salary, but by the end of every month his bank account was almost empty. He did not buy expensive things, so he could not understand the problem.\n\nHis older sister gave him some advice: \"For one month, write down everything you spend, even the smallest things.\" Jasur thought it was a boring idea, but he bought a small notebook and tried it.\n\nThe results surprised him. He spent almost a fifth of his money on taxis, because he often left home late and could not wait for the bus. He also bought coffee and snacks two or three times a day, and he was paying for three online services he had forgotten about.\n\nJasur did not want to live without any small pleasures, so he made a few realistic changes. He started getting up fifteen minutes earlier and took the bus to work. He cancelled two of the online services and brought a flask of tea from home. After three months, he had saved enough money for a short trip to Samarkand.\n\nNow Jasur recommends the notebook to all his friends. \"It is not about being mean with money,\" he says. \"It is about knowing where it goes.\"",
